Since //commit 0b62fe5e// OpenWrt can be installed using the [[docs:techref:bootloader:eva|EVA/Adam2 bootloader]]. Within the same HW revision 5 of the FRITZ!Box 3370 different NAND flash chips are used and the correct image has to be chosen.

**<color #ed1c24>Please read the detailed [[https://git.openwrt.org/?p=openwrt/openwrt.git;a=commit;h=0b62fe5ed87ecac52301096b15abb69f96117c8c|commit message]] before try install.</color>**

{{media:avm:fritzbox_3370:fritzbox_3370-rev5_micron.jpg?linkonly|Micron MT29F1G08ABADA NAND flash chip on AVM FRITZ!Box WLAN 3370}} -> 128MB NAND Flash Memory

{{:media:nand04gw3b2dn6_on_fritz3370.png?linkonly|ST-Micro NAND04GW3B2DN6 NAND flash chip on AVM FRITZ!Box WLAN 3370}} -> 512MB NAND Flash Memory\\
(works with hynix-image)

{{ :media:avm:fritzbox_3370:fritzbox.3370_hynix.hy27uf081g2m.nand.chip.jpg?linkonly |Hynix HY27UF081G2M NAND chip on AVM FRITZ!Box WLAN 3370}} -> 128MB NAND Flash Memory

generic hints: [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|install OpenWrt]] -> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing.ftp|flashing via FTP]]

==== Flash Layout ====

First let's have a quick view at the Flash Layout with the stock firmware and after OpenWrt has been installed. When you later want to understand, what mtd/sysupgrade do, have a second look here:

  * [[http://wiki.ip-phone-forum.de/software:ds-mod:development:flash#flash_partitionierung]]

